      "why": "Three independent bugs in different files; one touches CSP nonce handling (security-sensitive, risk floor). 138 test files present, so no safety-net bump.",
      "shared": "Run the relevant tests with: npx vitest --run <test file paths>\nDo not commit.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": "Case-insensitive Content-Type in parseBody and validator",
          "text": "`parseBody()` and `validator()` match Content-Type media types case-sensitively.\nA request with `Content-Type: Application/JSON` or\n`Application/X-WWW-Form-Urlencoded` is parsed fine by the platform Request,\nbut Hono's checks skip it and pass an empty object downstream. Media types are\ncase-insensitive (RFC 9110), so these requests should be parsed and validated\nlike their lower-case equivalents.",
          "tier": "standard",
          "effort": "medium",
          "risk_area": null,
          "why": "Clear spec, two call sites in one area; public API behavior but not a risk-floor code change; tests present."
        },
        {
          "title": "Compress middleware must not gzip 206 responses",
          "text": "The compress middleware gzips 206 Partial Content responses. The\nContent-Range header still describes the uncompressed byte range, and the\noriginal Content-Length is dropped, so clients that stitch ranges together\nget corrupted data. A 206 response should be passed through uncompressed.",
          "tier": "standard",
          "effort": "low",
          "risk_area": null,
          "why": "Single status-code check in one middleware with a clear expected behavior; tests present."
        },
        {
          "title": "Secure-headers nonce with both CSP modes",
          "text": "In the secure-headers middleware, using a nonce in one CSP mode breaks when\nboth `contentSecurityPolicy` and `contentSecurityPolicyReportOnly` are set:\nfor example a static enforced policy plus a report-only policy that uses a\nnonce. The request ends in a 500 response. Each policy should work\nindependently, including when both use nonces.",
          "tier": "deep",
          "effort": "medium",
          "risk_area": "security-sensitive code (CSP nonce handling)",
          "why": "Changes CSP nonce handling, which is security-sensitive and in the risk floor; tests present."
        }
      ]
    },
